DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       ggeettppeeeerrnnaammee()  returns  the address of the peer connected to the socket
       _s_o_c_k_f_d, in the buffer pointed to by _a_d_d_r.  The _a_d_d_r_l_e_n argument  should
       be  initialized to indicate the amount of space pointed to by _a_d_d_r.  On
       return it contains the actual size of the  name  returned  (in  bytes).
       The name is truncated if the buffer provided is too small.

       The  returned address is truncated if the buffer provided is too small;
       in this case, _a_d_d_r_l_e_n will return a value greater than was supplied  to
       the call.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEE
       On  success,  zero is returned.  On error, -1 is returned, and _e_r_r_n_o is
       set to indicate the error.

